{"book":21,"chapter":5,"context":{"chapter":5,"title":"Few Words Before God","summary":"Advice on worship (listen more than you speak, keep your vows) is followed by observations on corrupt officials, the restless money-lover, riches lost, and the gift of being able to enjoy what God gives.","background":"'The house of God' (v. 1) is the temple. Vows were voluntary promises to God, often of an offering, and the Law insisted they be kept (Deuteronomy 23:21-23). 'The angel' (v. 6) means 'messenger,' probably the priest who received what was vowed; Malachi 2:7 calls the priest 'the messenger of the Lord of hosts.'","customs":[{"term":"Higher than the highest","verses":"5:8","note":"Ancient kingdoms ran provinces through layers of officials, each answering to another above him and taking a share. The Preacher is not surprised by injustice in such a chain."}],"watchFor":["The working man sleeps sweetly; the rich man cannot (v. 12).","'Naked shall he return' (v. 15) echoes Job 1:21.","Being able to enjoy one's portion is 'the gift of God' (v. 19)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 23:21-23","Malachi 2:7","Job 1:21","1 Timothy 6:7-10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["שְׁמֹר","shemor","H8104","HVqv2ms","guard"],["רַגְלְךָ","ragleikha","H7272","HNcfsc/Sp2ms","foot your"],["כַּאֲשֶׁר","ka'asher","H834","HR/Tr","<just> when"],["תֵּלֵךְ","telekh","H1980","HVqi2ms","you will go"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["בֵּית","beit","H1004","HNcmsc","[the] house of"],["הָאֱלֹהִים","ha'elohim","H430","HTd/Ncmpa","<the> God"],["וְקָרוֹב","vekarov","H7126","HC/Vqaa","and draw near"],["לִשְׁמֹעַ","lishmoa'","H8085","HR/Vqcc","to listen"],["מִתֵּת","mitet","H5414","HR/Vqcc","more than giving"],["הַכְּסִילִים","hakesilim","H3684","HTd/Aampa","the fools"],["זָבַח","zavach","H2077","HNcmsa","a sacrifice"],["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","for"],["אֵינָם","'einam","H369","HNcmsc/Sp3mp","not they"],["יוֹדְעִים","yod'im","H3045","HVqrmpa","[are] knowing"],["לַעֲשׂוֹת","la'asot","H6213","HR/Vqcc","to do"],["רָע","